{"text": "Adjunct Staffer Loses Contract\n\nAnnette Rodriguez was\ntold she was no longer\nwelcome to teach at\nNorthern New Mexico\nCollege\n\nBy Ralph Chapoco\nSUN Staff Waiter\n\u2018When Northern New Mexico College\nadjunct faculty member Annette Rodriguez\neared she was not on the approved faculty\nlist, she wanted to know why, so she went\n\u2018on a quest to find the list, but was surprised\nby the outcome.\nRodriguez, was a beloved instructor at\nNorthern and she has the documentation to\nprove it, citing a letter that a student's\nmother wrote to the college\n\u201cShe was very patient\nways being there for him with advice,\nHenrietta Gaines wrote about Rodriguez. \u201cI\n\u2018want to thank her from the bottom of my\nheart for being there for my son as he un-\ndertakes his new joumey in his life,\n\nShe has also received very positive stu-\ndent evaluations. Moreover, Lori Franklin,\n\u2018an associate professor at Northem, raved\nabout her job performance. Franklin sent an\n\u2018email to Northern's Vice President of Insti-\ntutional Advancement Ricky Serna, advo-\nfing on Rodriguez's behalf,\n\u2018First of all, if I had been consulted, 1\ncould have verified that Annette has an ex-\ncellent record teaching as an adjunct for our\ndepartment,\u201d Franklin wrote, \u201cShe has nev-\n\u2018er neglected any of her responsibilities as an\nadjunct in any way. Also, [ have never re-\nceived a student complaint about Annette.\nTn fact, a student was just in my office last\nweek praising her abilities as an instructor.\nreview all student evaluations for my ad-\nJuncts, and she has received excellent ev\nuations every semester she has taught for\nNorther.\u201d\nBecause of her performance, Rodrignez,\nwas recommended to teach this summer as\npartof Northem\u2019s Summer Bridge program.\nShe signed the contract immediately and\nwaited for the hiring chair\u2019s signature so\nshe could begin teaching. The contract was\naot official until Patricia Trujillo signed it\nHowever, there were delays with the signa-\nture s0 Rodriguez could not begin teaching\n\nfor Summer Bridge.\nShe sent an email to Seraa on May 2 to\ninquire about the contract, He responded on\n\u2018May 7 and informed her she is not approved\n\u2018and would not be teaching at the college\nanymore, effectively terminating her em-\nployment.\n\u201cThe Personnel Action Form will not be\nsigned and fully executed,\u201d Serna wrote,\n\u201cYou are no longer on the list of approved\n\u2018adjunct faculty. Thank you.\u201d\nRodriguez was unaware that \u2018uch a list\nexisted, so she requested the document\nthrough the Inspection of Public Records\n\u2018Act on May 21. Brandi Cordova, North-\n\u2018ems public records custodian, responded\nJune 12 to the request.\n\u201cThis leters in response to your Inspec\ntion of Public Records Act request daied\nMay 21, 2014 in which you requested the\n\u201clist of approved adjunct faculty,\u201d Cordova\nwrote. \u201cPlease be advised that no such\ndocument exists.\u201d\n\u2018There is no formal list that names all\nadjunct faculty who are authorized to teach\nat the college. Instead, there were a serics of\n\nSes Tis on page At",
